Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.77,0:46:57.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm g show you some of the testing work.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:57.59,0:47:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the robots are basically built uh starting with the pelvis uh torso, head, arms, uh legs and hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:04.08,0:47:07.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we basically want to we want to go through like a basically a very
Dialogue: 0,0:47:07.42,0:47:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh strenuous testing process to make sure everything is like working nominally before we send it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:12.00,0:47:17.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we don't want any like loose cables or bad parts or bad communication.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:17.23,0:47:21.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we send the robot through what we call a final EOL test or end of line test.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:21.37,0:47:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is where the robots go through all the final checks and they basically go through also a burn-in on on these lines.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:27.52,0:47:28.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you mean by burnin?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:28.64,0:47:30.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,They'll they'll run for several hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.24,0:47:30.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.56,0:47:33.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we'll basically make sure there's nothing that basically uh no no issues pop
Dialogue: 0,0:47:34.03,0:47:37.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,up over those few hours before we before we send the send the robots out.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:37.68,0:47:43.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh so here we have um these bays that are running a combination
Dialogue: 0,0:47:43.25,0:47:47.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,of burn-in testing and uh and end ofline checks that we've designed here internally.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.72,0:47:53.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we basically go through a process where the robot's basically self like trying to understand itself like do is anything seem wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:53.80,0:47:55.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it is we will uh we'll flag it.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:55.91,0:47:59.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it's not basically we go through a process where we basically do like basically
Dialogue: 0,0:47:59.38,0:48:03.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,a bunch of checks and burn in make sure the robot's in good good condition.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:03.44,0:48:10.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um if they pass here we basically uh we'll we'll walk over to headquarters and if they fail here we need to go fix it and understand why.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:10.32,0:48:12.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why do these ones have vests on them?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:12.96,0:48:15.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, when the robots are getting brought up,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:15.21,0:48:24.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,we basically uh we I think we hold it through a gantry system on the back and they have their vests on for that system.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:24.32,0:48:27.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's basically like the robots are like just been born and they're waking up.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:27.28,0:48:30.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're saying, you know, they look at they look at their hands,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.15,0:48:37.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,they start calibrating itself visually and um try trying to make sure everything's in a healthy state of this campus.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.52,0:48:42.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,What is your favorite part?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:42.32,0:48:44.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think Baku is one of my favorite parts here.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.47,0:48:46.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like being able to build robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:46.64,0:48:51.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um in March we had record um you know we we we had record manufacturing.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:51.88,0:48:57.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we we we made more robots in March than we had ever in our entire lifetime combined.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.31,0:49:00.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it's just cool to see us being able to do this and then get them out the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:00.80,0:49:05.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so I would say um this is probably one of my favorite places in the in the campus.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:05.66,0:49:09.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think maybe my other favorite place that we'll show um some point here is like
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.81,0:49:15.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,the robots doing real useful work 247 um on our either commercial customers or in the home.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:15.77,0:49:20.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that stuff is just amazing because what we're here to do is we're here to like basically build like uh humanlike
Dialogue: 0,0:49:20.77,0:49:26.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,intelligence in the world and to see robots working 247 being able to do things like humans can is like so special.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:26.47,0:49:27.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like such a hard thing to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.68,0:49:27.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.93,0:49:32.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And be able to see us doing it like uh at these levels of reliability is like it's awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.31,0:49:35.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so I think it's probably a couple of my favorite places on campus.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.52,0:49:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you didn't have your job, what job would you want here?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.92,0:49:45.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think um I think there's a few things I really like.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.57,0:49:51.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like the engineering design process of how do you think about clean sheet improving the system to be like more reliable,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.79,0:49:58.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,cheaper, lower in mass and um overall a better functioning robot that can do more of what humans can with less complexity.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:58.53,0:50:05.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that that job across the hardware like engineering and software engineering design or is like I I spent a lot of time
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.02,0:50:12.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,in that uh like leading engineering here and it's just like a uh yeah it's just a really fun and I think very hard problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:12.83,0:50:17.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh everything you try every choice you make to try to make the robot better for thermals or
Dialogue: 0,0:50:17.22,0:50:22.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,better like lower lower mass or like lower weight makes the something else on the other side worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.26,0:50:27.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like if you're trying to make the robot like lighter it means it probably can't like hold as much weight. then can't hold as much weight.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:27.75,0:50:32.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,The customers are like, "Well, if you can't carry 30 pound boxes around, I I can't use you on this assembly line."
Dialogue: 0,0:50:33.02,0:50:38.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so there's just like um I think there's a lot of just interesting, very hard problems to solve there.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.08,0:50:44.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think second is like how do we get neural networks to run on robots and generalize at scale on the Helix team
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.48,0:50:51.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,and that for uh really is like a um at this point a data and generalization issue and that's a really hard fun problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:51.43,0:50:54.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh manufacturing is another one of how do we like how do we manufacture robots at scale?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:54.96,0:50:57.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we continue to get robots in the manufacturing process to build themselves?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:58.02,0:51:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how do we get them to off the lines into the real world as fast as possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.00,0:51:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,At some point here, it'll just be like a it'll just be full lights out manufacturing.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:06.80,0:51:09.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we'll have like robots only building robots and sending out to the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:09.56,0:51:11.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,The robots will be getting into boxes themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.31,0:51:15.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Other robots will be boxing them up and we'll be shipping them out to customers.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.44,0:51:15.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.92,0:51:17.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sounds a bit sentient.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:17.84,0:51:18.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a bit sentient.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:18.77,0:51:19.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:19.04,0:51:23.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh so that's another area where I'm just like um it's extremely interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:23.28,0:51:27.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think the last piece is uh um we have a whole commercial operations team
Dialogue: 0,0:51:27.28,0:51:30.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's trying to get robots out to the world at scale and make them really useful.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:30.54,0:51:35.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we did this uh with BMW last year and we're doing it with more customers this year for figure three.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:35.76,0:51:40.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's um it's a really cool problem because it's really hard like robots need to get in the environment needs to get safely.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.80,0:51:44.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,They never like basically can almost never fault and when they do fault they need to understand
Dialogue: 0,0:51:44.28,0:51:48.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,that and self-correct and then we need to be able to do useful human work at human performance.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.58,0:51:54.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,So our our comparison is like what does a human do today in terms of speeds inaccuracies um and then reliability.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:54.59,0:51:56.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like that's a hard bar to hit.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:56.26,0:52:04.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh those are all like um kind of like gigantic problems to go solve that I think I if I was you know here I'd want to spend all my time on those.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:04.80,0:52:05.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:05.28,0:52:05.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:05.62,0:52:06.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:06.13,0:52:06.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
